6 0 obj
<< /Length 2892 >>
stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 56 752 Td (PM-2025-019: month-end batch contention on core-banking-db) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 716 Td (1. Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 694 Td (On 31 July 2025 the month-end interest posting batch started at 19:30 UTC instead of 23:00) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 680 Td (UTC, because a manual re-run was triggered after a failure earlier in the day. It ran) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 666 Td (alongside evening peak traffic. The batch opened over 300 database sessions and held row) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 652 Td (locks on the balances table. Login and balance requests slowed to 5 to 8 times their normal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 638 Td (latency for 50 minutes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 602 Td (2. Impact) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 580 Td (- Login p95 latency up to 8 times normal; balance checks up to 6 times normal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 566 Td (- Error rate peaked at 7%, mostly timeouts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 552 Td (- 95 complaints about slow login and balances not loading.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 538 Td (- No incorrect postings.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 502 Td (3. Timeline \(UTC\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 480 Td (- 19:30 Manual re-run of the interest posting batch started.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 466 Td (- 19:34 Database connections reached 96% of the maximum; lock waits rose sharply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 452 Td (- 19:38 Latency alerts for auth-service and accounts-service.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 438 Td (- 19:55 Responders found the batch sessions in the database session list.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 424 Td (- 20:05 Batch paused with the batch owner's agreement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 410 Td (- 20:20 Latency back to normal. Batch resumed at 23:00 and finished normally.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 374 Td (4. Root cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 352 Td (The re-run bypassed the scheduler's batch window check, so a heavy batch ran during peak) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 338 Td (hours. The batch and the online services share one connection limit, so the batch took most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 324 Td (of the connections and its row locks blocked balance reads.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 288 Td (5. Lessons) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 266 Td (- Responders first suspected a mobile app release from earlier that day, which delayed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252 Td (   the diagnosis by about 15 minutes. The release had no database access.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 238 Td (- Pausing the batch was safe and fast; killing sessions was considered but rejected) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 224 Td (   because it could leave postings half-applied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 188 Td (6. Actions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 166 Td (- Manual batch re-runs now go through the same batch window check.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 152 Td (- Batch workloads moved to a separate connection pool with a hard session limit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 138 Td (- Any change to batch schedules needs a review against the peak-hours calendar.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
